# Force LF for anything that will run on macOS / Linux — CRLF at end of a bash
# script produces `\r`-terminated tokens that break early with cryptic errors
# ("bad interpreter", `: command not found`, etc.). Windows tools tolerate LF
# fine, so this is safe everywhere.
mac/**             text eol=lf
*.sh               text eol=lf
*.command          text eol=lf
